[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: delegation.DELEGATION
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[DELEGATION]
overview: Automatic decomposition of tasks into subagents to save context tokens and route work by cost
purpose: Main agent stays focused on synthesis; cheap/mechanical work goes to cheaper models; large tool outputs never pollute main context
mechanism: Before starting any task, main agent checks triggers → picks model via routing matrix → spawns subagent with self-contained prompt and response budget → integrates summary

[CORE_PRINCIPLE]
The main agent's context is the most expensive resource. Protect it.
Every tool call that returns >1k tokens, every multi-file scan, every long log read
is a candidate for delegation. The question is never "can I do this myself" —
it is "does doing this myself leak tokens the main thread will need later".

[QUICK_START]
1. Before tool use: Estimate output size and task complexity
2. Check: Do triggers in TRIGGERS.toon fire? → if yes, delegate
3. Route: Pick model via ROUTING.toon (haiku for mechanical, sonnet for standard, opus for synthesis)
4. Shape: Use a template from PATTERNS.toon; always set a response word-budget
5. Filter: Confirm not in ANTI_PATTERNS.toon
6. Spawn: Call Agent() with model, self-contained prompt, and budget
7. Integrate: Read subagent summary; do NOT re-do work it already did

[DOCUMENTATION_STRUCTURE]
Small modular files in docs/agent/delegation/:
  → TRIGGERS.toon          When delegation is required (criteria with thresholds)
  → ROUTING.toon           Model↔task matrix (haiku / sonnet / opus)
  → PATTERNS.toon          Ready-to-use Agent() invocation templates
  → ANTI_PATTERNS.toon     When NOT to delegate (overhead > savings)
  → BUDGETS.toon           Token/cost thresholds and response-length rules

[WHY_THIS_MATTERS]
- Context window is finite; once polluted with raw tool output, later tasks degrade
- Haiku is ~5× cheaper than Sonnet; mechanical work routed to Haiku is a pure win
- Independent subtasks run in parallel → wall-clock wins
- Subagent summaries are naturally terse → the main thread retains only decisions, not logs

[NEXT_STEPS]
Start here: → TRIGGERS.toon (learn when to delegate)
Then: → ROUTING.toon (learn which model for which task)
Then: → PATTERNS.toon (copy-paste-ready invocations)
Finally: → BUDGETS.toon (enforce response budgets)
